WEBVTT

00:01.680 --> 00:06.190
<i>Well, it's second and last day of 
the Patissier World Tournament,</i>

00:06.190 --> 00:08.400
<i>and we've come to the grand finale!</i>

00:11.110 --> 00:12.420
Incredible.

00:12.420 --> 00:16.030
It's no wonder they call him 
the Patissier Chosen One.

00:16.030 --> 00:17.570
It's magnificent!

00:18.530 --> 00:21.050
The final round is "candy sculpture."

00:21.050 --> 00:25.060
He'll be named the world's 
greatest patissier for sure!

00:35.690 --> 00:38.170
<i>It's like a land of sweets.</i>

00:40.790 --> 00:46.190
<i>I'm going to win this and achieve the 
dream I've had since I was a child!</i>

00:48.000 --> 00:51.860
<i>They're moving their finished 
pieces to the judging area now.</i>

00:53.820 --> 00:55.080
Let's go.

00:55.080 --> 00:57.410
One, two, three!

01:15.540 --> 01:16.960
<i>Wait, am I...</i>

01:17.370 --> 01:20.010
<i>Ah, am I dying?</i>

01:21.800 --> 01:25.730
<i>I wanted to create the world's 
greatest sweets before I died...</i>

01:26.310 --> 01:29.480
<i>I wanted to use them to 
create a land of sweets,</i>

01:29.480 --> 01:32.660
<i>and bring smiles to the faces 
of everyone in the world.</i>

01:33.010 --> 01:34.350
<i>Now, I never will.</i>

01:34.350 --> 01:37.240
<i>God... you are far too cruel.</i>

01:37.720 --> 01:42.300
<i>Then allow me to grant you one more chance!</i>

01:42.970 --> 01:44.900
<i>Huh? Who's there?</i>

01:46.670 --> 01:49.100
<i>Your new name shall be...</i>

01:49.500 --> 01:51.870
<i>Pastry Mille Morteln!</i>

02:10.020 --> 02:12.610
<b>Sweet Reincarnation</b>

03:34.800 --> 03:36.090
<i>The Fief of Morteln.</i>

03:35.040 --> 03:40.440
<b>Dreaming of a Land of Sweets</b>

03:36.590 --> 03:40.440
<i>I heard that when my father, Casserole Mille 
Morteln, first became its suzerain lord,</i>

03:41.170 --> 03:44.940
<i>it was a barren land that 
could barely grow wheat.</i>

03:47.480 --> 03:50.280
<i>My father worked hard beside 
those who moved there with him,</i>

03:50.280 --> 03:53.240
<i>and those already living there.</i>

03:53.240 --> 03:57.470
<i>Together, they spent almost twenty 
years cultivating the soil.</i>

03:59.180 --> 04:00.830
<i>That hard work paid off,</i>

04:00.830 --> 04:05.650
<i>and we've managed to grow to a fief of 
three villages of about forty people each,</i>

04:05.650 --> 04:07.630
<i>capable of growing both wheat and barley.</i>

04:08.600 --> 04:10.950
C'mon! You'll need to do better than that!

04:10.950 --> 04:12.520
I haven't gotten started!

04:17.080 --> 04:20.440
<b>Pastry Mille Morteln</b>

04:20.760 --> 04:22.900
You're getting sloppy with your grip again.

04:22.900 --> 04:23.970
Yes, sir...

04:27.120 --> 04:30.780
<i>It's been nine years since I was reincarnated
 as the son of the fief's suzerain lord,</i>

04:29.390 --> 04:33.250
<b>Father  Casserole</b>

04:30.780 --> 04:31.910
<i>Lord Casserole.</i>

04:33.250 --> 04:37.550
Yes! Hold it so tight, I could tear 
off your hands before you'd let go!

04:38.250 --> 04:38.710
Yes, sir!

04:41.570 --> 04:44.890
<i>I was raised by my father—
a military hero—my kind mother,</i>

04:45.250 --> 04:47.520
<i>and my five older sisters.</i>

04:47.520 --> 04:49.170
<i>It's basically been a happy life, but...</i>

04:50.140 --> 04:50.990
<i>But...</i>

04:52.370 --> 04:57.310
<i>Our fief can't grow sugar, and it's 
hard to get sweet things here.</i>

04:58.220 --> 05:01.340
<i>Gosh, I sure do wanna make sweets!</i>

05:01.340 --> 05:02.390
Don't get distracted!

05:07.200 --> 05:09.660
<b>Head Retainer  Feuille</b>

05:07.410 --> 05:09.660
There you are! Hey, Boss!

05:09.940 --> 05:11.800
Hard at work, I see.

05:12.170 --> 05:15.040
It'll be time for breakfast soon, you know.

05:15.040 --> 05:17.370
Right. We'll end here for now.

05:17.710 --> 05:19.000
Yes, sir.

05:19.000 --> 05:21.840
Thank you... very much.

05:21.840 --> 05:24.000
How can I help you, Feuille?

05:24.000 --> 05:26.180
I've got good news and bad news for you.

05:26.530 --> 05:28.090
Which do you want first?

05:28.090 --> 05:30.900
Since I'll have to hear both either way,

05:30.900 --> 05:32.890
let's start with the good.

05:32.890 --> 05:34.190
Well, then...

05:34.190 --> 05:38.350
It's looking like the bean fields will 
yield a significant harvest this year.

05:38.990 --> 05:41.070
It all worked out like the kid said.

05:41.420 --> 05:44.990
Sprinkling lime on the soil 
improves the crop yield!

05:44.990 --> 05:48.010
Looks like I was right to take your advice.

05:48.770 --> 05:50.780
We'll have a bumper bean crop this year...

05:50.590 --> 05:57.500
<b>talk talk</b>

05:50.590 --> 05:57.500
<b>talk talk</b>

05:51.070 --> 05:53.480
We'll be limited to simple 
bean dishes for now,

05:53.480 --> 05:56.460
but caramelized roasted soybeans 
are a classic tea snack,

05:56.460 --> 05:59.700
and you can sprinkle soybean flour 
on them for extra flavor.

05:59.700 --> 06:01.680
How do you know all that?

06:02.550 --> 06:05.420
Oh! Just more daydreams.

06:02.550 --> 06:05.740
<i>I can't exactly tell them it's 
because I was reincarnated.</i>

06:06.170 --> 06:10.940
Well, it certainly wouldn't 
be your first flight of fancy.

06:11.350 --> 06:14.170
But the ideas you pull from 
that imagination of yours

06:14.170 --> 06:18.050
have made good policy for the 
fief these past few years.

06:18.050 --> 06:20.450
Like a little shadow suzerain!

06:21.880 --> 06:24.610
So, what's the bad news?

06:26.510 --> 06:30.950
It seems that attempts to stamp out bandits 
in the County of Retes have failed.

06:32.010 --> 06:33.170
Bandits?!

06:33.170 --> 06:36.120
I'm told the stragglers have 
escaped and are heading our way.

06:36.120 --> 06:36.910
How many?

06:36.910 --> 06:38.620
About fifty.

06:39.450 --> 06:42.330
<i>If bandits come here, 
they'll ravage our fields.</i>

06:42.920 --> 06:46.590
<i>Both the beans we worked so hard for,
 and the precious wheat...</i>

06:47.380 --> 06:50.330
They'll likely arrive in two months' time.

06:50.790 --> 06:52.220
Two months, eh?

06:52.450 --> 06:54.730
Our only chance is to round up the villagers

06:54.730 --> 06:57.990
and drive the bandits off with pikes and slings.

06:58.360 --> 07:00.150
<i>Even if we pull from all three villages,</i>

07:00.150 --> 07:01.770
<i>we'll get thirty men at most.</i>

07:02.580 --> 07:04.510
<i>We'll barely be able to 
slow the bandits down.</i>

07:05.220 --> 07:07.990
<i>And in a prolonged battle, 
we're doomed for sure.</i>

07:08.650 --> 07:10.130
This village has the canal.

07:10.130 --> 07:11.980
What if we hole up here to buy time,

07:12.470 --> 07:16.050
while I ask Count Retes for reinforcements?

07:16.400 --> 07:18.690
Knowing you, you could do it.

07:18.690 --> 07:19.950
The only issue is...

07:20.540 --> 07:23.330
Count Retes's reputation.

07:23.330 --> 07:27.450
If we were to defeat bandits that the 
County failed to stamp out completely,

07:27.450 --> 07:30.720
it would subject the Count to 
accusations of incompetence.

07:31.050 --> 07:34.650
We won't be getting reinforcements 
from there, then.

07:35.300 --> 07:37.120
The ideal outcome for the Count

07:37.120 --> 07:42.390
would be for us to fail so that the 
Margravate of Hubarek has to clean up for us...

07:39.810 --> 07:45.080
<i>Father has three resident retainers,
 including Feuille.</i>

07:45.570 --> 07:47.280
<i>It won't be an easy fight.</i>

07:48.170 --> 07:51.310
<i>But the beans... and most 
of all, the wheat...</i>

07:51.310 --> 07:53.790
<i>I need them all for making sweets!</i>

07:53.790 --> 07:55.450
<i>Anyone who'd try to take that from me...</i>

07:59.130 --> 08:01.640
<i>Looking good, kid!</i>

08:01.640 --> 08:05.650
<i>He's starting to feel his calling 
as this fief's next suzerain lord.</i>

08:06.680 --> 08:11.590
<i>Anyone who gets in the way of my dream... 
My plan to create a land of sweets...</i>

08:12.380 --> 08:14.510
<i>I'll make them regret it!</i>

08:15.360 --> 08:20.020
One way or another, we're gonna 
have to make a big gamble.

08:20.020 --> 08:22.680
This is just my instinct talking,

08:22.680 --> 08:26.790
but how's about we wager on 
the kid as our trump card?

08:26.790 --> 08:27.610
Pas, a trump card?

08:27.610 --> 08:31.690
If the gamble pays off, he might 
be as useful as you are, Boss.

08:31.690 --> 08:34.560
I'd never dare question your instinct,

08:34.560 --> 08:36.440
but you're effectively hoping for magi—

08:38.360 --> 08:39.660
The Sanctification Ceremony!

08:39.660 --> 08:40.930
Exactly!

08:43.590 --> 08:46.790
Agnes, Josephine. Listen to me.

08:47.360 --> 08:50.150
I'm going to put Pas through 
the Sanctification Ceremony.

08:50.150 --> 08:50.880
Dear?!

08:51.270 --> 08:54.170
Surely it's much too soon for Pas.

08:51.320 --> 08:55.070
<b>Mother  Agnes</b>

08:54.170 --> 08:56.990
You know as well as I do 
how bright the boy is.

08:57.490 --> 09:00.890
He's at the top of his age 
group with a sword, as well.

09:01.150 --> 09:02.100
But...

09:02.370 --> 09:06.560
I deem him accomplished with 
both the pen and the sword.

09:06.850 --> 09:10.450
<i>The Sanctification Ceremony is 
this world's coming-of-age ritual.</i>

09:07.000 --> 09:11.550
<b>Big Sister  Josephine</b>

09:10.890 --> 09:13.940
<i>I'm only nine, so it </i>is<i> a 
bit early for me, but...</i>

09:14.400 --> 09:15.650
<i>It's just what I want!</i>

09:16.150 --> 09:18.780
<i>Still... it's a real shock for Mother.</i>

09:18.200 --> 09:21.300
If you deem him worthy, I cannot argue.

09:19.480 --> 09:22.730
<i>The ritual is usually for those between 
thirteen and fifteen years old.</i>

09:23.730 --> 09:27.690
I'd hoped for more time 
with him as a child, but...

09:28.350 --> 09:30.280
We set out in three days' time.

09:30.280 --> 09:31.630
Make the preparations.

09:31.630 --> 09:32.670
All right.

09:33.530 --> 09:35.690
Josie! Help me out with that, would you?

09:35.690 --> 09:37.380
Why, certainly, Mother!

09:37.720 --> 09:42.350
He's got to represent the 
family <i>perfectly</i>, after all...

09:42.350 --> 09:45.310
That's right. He's got to be <i>perfect<i>

09:45.660 --> 09:49.270
<b>Heh heh heh...</b></i></i>

09:45.660 --> 09:49.270
<b>Heh heh heh...</b>

09:46.610 --> 09:49.270
<i>Not good... Nothing goes well 
when they smile like that!</i>

09:49.270 --> 09:50.810
F-Father!

09:50.810 --> 09:52.320
I'm eating.

09:52.320 --> 09:54.610
<i>Father!</i>

09:54.840 --> 09:57.320
So cute!

09:57.650 --> 09:59.580
W-Wait a minute!

09:59.580 --> 10:01.670
Don't you see how wrong this is?!

10:01.670 --> 10:04.100
It looks lovely on you, Pas!

10:04.100 --> 10:06.410
These shoes might be perfect!

10:06.410 --> 10:09.220
Josie, aren't those your precious shoes—

10:09.220 --> 10:10.090
No big deal!

10:10.090 --> 10:12.310
Only the best for my sweet little brother!

10:12.310 --> 10:14.880
Are you two listening to me at all?!

10:12.870 --> 10:14.880
Now let's do his makeup!

10:15.190 --> 10:17.850
Skin like yours takes to makeup so well!

10:17.850 --> 10:19.180
<i>I guess they're not...</i>

10:20.170 --> 10:25.230
<i>Ever since I was little, my mother and 
sister have treated me like a dress-up doll.</i>

10:26.650 --> 10:28.770
<i>Back when my other older sisters were around,</i>

10:28.830 --> 10:31.730
<b>Eldest Sister{top right, counter-clockwise}</b>

10:29.080 --> 10:31.730
<b>Second Sister</b>

10:29.330 --> 10:31.730
<b>Third Sister</b>

10:29.390 --> 10:31.730
<i>it was even worse!</i>

10:29.580 --> 10:31.730
<b>Fourth Sister</b>

10:29.830 --> 10:31.730
<b>Fifth Sister</b>

10:30.080 --> 10:31.730
<b>Eldest Brother{blue}</b>

10:32.040 --> 10:34.550
<i>It looks best on him out of everyone here!</i>

10:34.550 --> 10:35.690
<i>Father!</i>

10:36.040 --> 10:39.710
<i>I want to be an adult ASAP!</i>

10:43.150 --> 10:44.620
What's the matter, son of mine?

10:45.070 --> 10:48.580
How are you so exhausted on 
the day of our departure?

10:48.580 --> 10:51.580
It's been a busy three days.

10:53.460 --> 10:54.540
Pas...

10:56.580 --> 10:57.720
Take care.

10:57.720 --> 10:59.030
Give it your best!

10:59.030 --> 10:59.760
I will!

10:59.760 --> 11:01.940
Hey, Pas!

11:01.940 --> 11:04.220
Marc! Lumi! Guys!

11:04.220 --> 11:06.890
You lucky duck! The capital, huh?

11:04.910 --> 11:09.620
<b>Luminito</b>

11:04.910 --> 11:09.620
<b>Marcarullo</b>

11:06.890 --> 11:09.670
I wish I could go too, dressed 
up in a fancy suit like yours!

11:09.670 --> 11:12.250
Nah, you'd look awful in one.

11:12.250 --> 11:14.230
What the hell'd you just say?!

11:14.230 --> 11:16.440
Take care on your trip, Pas!

11:16.880 --> 11:17.610
Sure.

11:17.610 --> 11:20.400
I'll eat lots of delicious 
things while I'm gone!

11:20.680 --> 11:22.500
He's all about food. Typical!

11:22.500 --> 11:24.370
Well, that's our Pas!

11:24.970 --> 11:26.160
Look after things here.

11:26.160 --> 11:26.950
Sure.

12:07.150 --> 12:09.080
Awesome!

12:09.080 --> 12:12.330
Lord Casserole's magic really is incredible.

12:13.540 --> 12:14.380
Josie...

12:14.380 --> 12:16.330
Yes, Mother.

12:16.830 --> 12:19.770
Pas still looks best in women's clothing!

12:20.960 --> 12:23.430
<b>Capital City  Bovaldia</b>

12:23.890 --> 12:25.640
That's the capital for you!

12:25.640 --> 12:29.540
<i>This is the most people I've ever seen 
in one place since my reincarnation!</i>

12:30.300 --> 12:34.020
Father! There's so many things 
here I've never seen before!

12:34.680 --> 12:36.230
<i>Is that brown sugar?!</i>

12:36.230 --> 12:38.190
<i>And fruit?!</i>

12:38.580 --> 12:42.610
<i>The Fief of Morteln has so few sweet things. 
I never see any of this stuff there!</i>

12:43.120 --> 12:44.650
<i>With all that at my disposal...</i>

12:45.090 --> 12:49.610
<i>Brown sugar cookies, pound cake,
 chocolate gâteau, flan!</i>

12:50.290 --> 12:53.120
<i>I'm raring to go! My blood is racing!</i>

12:53.120 --> 12:54.070
Okay.

12:54.070 --> 12:56.750
If you can make it through 
the Sanctifiction Ceremony

12:56.750 --> 12:59.090
I'll buy you whatever you like.

12:59.090 --> 13:00.390
You mean it?!

13:00.390 --> 13:01.930
Yes!

13:01.930 --> 13:03.770
Oh, but I can't choose!

13:03.770 --> 13:05.550
What should I ask for?

13:06.840 --> 13:08.010
<i>Are those...</i>

13:08.010 --> 13:09.270
<i>apples?!</i>

13:09.270 --> 13:11.040
<i>And they look so delicious!</i>

13:11.040 --> 13:13.730
<i>I'm so glad they exist in this world, too!</i>

13:13.730 --> 13:15.590
Those are bonkas, I believe.

13:15.590 --> 13:16.440
Bonkas?

13:16.440 --> 13:19.040
They're grown up north,

13:19.040 --> 13:21.400
so it's rare to see them in the market here.

13:21.640 --> 13:25.570
They're on the sour side, though I haven't
 had much of them myself.

13:26.570 --> 13:28.270
<i>Sour, huh?</i>

13:28.270 --> 13:31.330
<i>There's all kinds of ways to use sour apples!</i>

13:31.710 --> 13:35.010
Father! I'd like to try growing bonkas!

13:35.010 --> 13:36.100
Growing them?

13:36.100 --> 13:38.040
Let's bring some back with us!

13:38.410 --> 13:39.530
Really?

13:40.320 --> 13:42.650
<i>Seeing him interested in 
the goods of other lands...</i>

13:43.280 --> 13:46.010
<i>He's developing the instincts 
of a true suzerain!</i>

13:46.330 --> 13:49.830
<i>If I got five of them, I could 
try all kinds of things...</i>

13:55.110 --> 13:57.940
<i>I'd love to try them glacé, but...</i>

13:58.340 --> 14:02.040
<i>Sugar itself is such a luxury! 
I'm sure it's too much to ask.</i>

14:03.290 --> 14:05.360
<i>What if we raised bees in our fief,</i>

14:05.640 --> 14:08.320
<i>and I candied them in honey instead?</i>

14:08.730 --> 14:09.530
<i>Tarts!</i>

14:09.810 --> 14:10.820
<i>Baked apples!</i>

14:11.150 --> 14:13.040
<i>And the old classic, apple pie!</i>

14:14.450 --> 14:17.460
<i>With talent like his, if he 
were to inherit the fief...</i>

14:18.220 --> 14:22.250
<i>If I can cultivate apples, 
and then inherit the fief...</i>

14:23.150 --> 14:24.840
<i>A rich land with a strong army!</i>

14:25.450 --> 14:27.850
<i>A land full of all the sweets you can eat!</i>

14:29.300 --> 14:30.230
We're here.

14:33.760 --> 14:36.310
Well, well, if it isn't the Lord of Morteln.

14:36.560 --> 14:38.390
Thank you for coming all this way.

14:37.370 --> 14:38.390
<i>A panda?!</i>

14:38.600 --> 14:41.350
Father. It's an honor to see you again.

14:41.350 --> 14:45.470
We last met at your daughter's 
Sanctification Ceremony, I believe.

14:45.470 --> 14:47.820
You did me a great service that day.

14:47.820 --> 14:50.490
I've heard many tales of you, milord.

14:50.490 --> 14:55.160
For instance, that you protected your 
people through the last year's frost.

14:55.430 --> 14:59.420
Thanks only to the protection 
of God and the Spirits...

14:59.420 --> 15:01.640
And my son's wisdom, as well.

15:02.690 --> 15:04.460
And you've brought your son today, have you?

15:04.720 --> 15:09.930
I'd like him to undergo his 
Sanctification Ceremony today.

15:09.930 --> 15:11.230
What?!

15:11.230 --> 15:13.640
Do you mean this, milord?

15:13.920 --> 15:14.850
I certainly do.

15:14.850 --> 15:17.850
And I'd like it to be a True Sanctification.

15:22.520 --> 15:23.860
Hey, Feuille.

15:23.860 --> 15:27.480
"True Sanctification" is the ceremony 
where you get magic, right?

15:27.480 --> 15:28.750
Oh, yeah.

15:28.750 --> 15:31.450
The one the kid's going to undergo?

15:31.450 --> 15:34.680
When I went for my Ceremony,

15:34.680 --> 15:36.860
they said I didn't have much magic power,

15:36.860 --> 15:39.300
so I didn't get to go through that one.

15:39.660 --> 15:42.000
I hope Pas will be okay.

15:42.000 --> 15:44.520
I think he'll be fine, little lady.

15:44.520 --> 15:46.240
What do they do for it?

15:46.240 --> 15:49.090
Well, it's like...

15:49.850 --> 15:53.800
They measure how much magic 
power you've got, and then...

16:02.290 --> 16:04.240
Now, imbibe this.

16:08.530 --> 16:09.890
<i>I-It's bitter!</i>

16:10.200 --> 16:11.740
<i>Wh-What the hell is this stuff?!</i>

16:12.090 --> 16:13.320
What then?

16:13.320 --> 16:14.780
You don't do anything.

16:15.500 --> 16:17.120
You don't do <i>anything</i>?!

16:19.050 --> 16:21.430
You're left alone in the dark,

16:22.040 --> 16:25.000
unable to see or hear anything

16:25.000 --> 16:26.050
for hours and hours...

16:28.810 --> 16:33.420
Magic is a grand power 
hidden inside a person.

16:33.420 --> 16:36.130
This is the only way to draw it out—

16:36.920 --> 16:41.270
To face hardship and endure, all by yourself.

16:51.050 --> 16:53.110
It's been a day and a half now.

16:54.200 --> 16:56.430
Surely it's taking too long...

16:56.430 --> 17:01.620
We cannot release your son until 
the radiance subsides, I fear.

17:02.240 --> 17:05.580
That said, it is impressive that 
the moment has not yet come.

17:05.910 --> 17:10.550
How much power does that 
boy have hidden within him?

17:11.010 --> 17:13.640
Do you think he'll be all right?

17:14.010 --> 17:19.600
Certainly, so much time in darkness 
and silence would be trying for most.

17:20.070 --> 17:21.220
Pas...

17:22.500 --> 17:23.450
<i>What will I...</i>

17:24.210 --> 17:26.690
<i>What will I make with those bonkas?!</i>

17:26.690 --> 17:29.380
<i>Just imagine! Someday, 
I'll find a way to get sugar.</i>

17:29.380 --> 17:30.620
<i>And then...</i>

17:30.620 --> 17:34.440
<i>It's hard to feel stressed when 
I'm thinking about sweets!</i>

17:34.440 --> 17:36.700
<i>I'm overflowing with glee!</i>

17:38.430 --> 17:41.570
<i>I want to fill this world with sweets,</i>

17:41.570 --> 17:43.260
<i>and bring smiles to everyone's faces!</i>

17:43.790 --> 17:46.170
<i>I want to make the world's best sweets!</i>

17:47.180 --> 17:51.090
<i>That must have been the reason 
I was born into this world!</i>

17:53.590 --> 17:55.140
<i>To create this world's...</i>

17:56.460 --> 17:58.850
<i>This world's very own land of sweets!</i>

18:03.560 --> 18:04.350
<i>What's that?</i>

18:05.870 --> 18:07.170
<i>H-Hey!</i>

18:19.000 --> 18:21.460
Is this... magic?

18:22.630 --> 18:23.770
Pas!

18:26.830 --> 18:27.750
Pas!

18:28.270 --> 18:29.330
Father?

18:29.940 --> 18:31.470
You endured it admirably.

18:31.470 --> 18:32.670
Two whole days!

18:32.670 --> 18:34.110
Two days?

18:34.110 --> 18:35.380
It's been that long?

18:35.940 --> 18:40.840
<i>I had so many dreams... 
but I can't remember now.</i>

18:42.240 --> 18:45.270
Now, we'll bring this to a close.

18:45.270 --> 18:47.890
If you've truly found your power within,

18:47.890 --> 18:52.520
then the scripture I'm about to 
read should have meaning to you.

18:52.520 --> 18:58.010
With this blessing of scripture, the 
Sanctification Ceremony will come to an end.

18:58.010 --> 18:58.650
Yes, sir.

18:58.650 --> 19:03.660
Vast though this world might be, 
and rich with myriad forms of life,

19:03.660 --> 19:07.020
it all receiveth equally 
those blessings divine.

19:07.020 --> 19:14.540
So, too, do its people receive the 
immeasurable bounties of our most holy God.

19:14.540 --> 19:18.760
Thou, who art Pastry Mil Morteln,

19:19.090 --> 19:22.330
with gratitude in thy heart 
for God's beneficent favor,

19:22.330 --> 19:25.290
receivest thou now God's blessings...

19:29.270 --> 19:32.400
<i>What... What I can do...</i>

19:35.310 --> 19:37.650
<i>R-Reincarnation?</i>

19:38.580 --> 19:39.750
<i>Replication?</i>

19:40.200 --> 19:41.820
<i>This must be...</i>

19:44.890 --> 19:46.950
<i>The scripture itself is...</i>

19:48.220 --> 19:49.240
<i>the magic?</i>

20:09.930 --> 20:10.880
Pas!

20:11.460 --> 20:13.310
Looks like you made it through.

20:15.750 --> 20:21.150
It appears you've acquired power nearly 
unheard of in this day and age!

20:21.420 --> 20:23.440
I can't thank you enough for your aid.

20:23.780 --> 20:25.820
A humble token of my gratitude.

20:26.630 --> 20:29.330
Many thanks to you, milord!

20:29.540 --> 20:33.270
The Church appreciates your 
most generous donation.

20:33.270 --> 20:37.560
May your son's future 
rest safe in God's hands.

20:44.500 --> 20:46.310
Pas, are you done yet?

20:46.310 --> 20:48.430
This one's heavier...

20:48.430 --> 20:50.600
but this one's more lustrous...

20:50.600 --> 20:53.310
But these are tempting, too!

20:53.610 --> 20:56.090
You need to choose already.

20:56.730 --> 20:57.940
Yes, sir.

20:59.610 --> 21:02.820
I'll throw in a few extra. 
For your enthusiasm!

21:02.820 --> 21:04.280
Here!

21:04.280 --> 21:05.490
You sure?!

21:07.020 --> 21:08.810
<i>The best-looking ones yet!</i>

21:09.570 --> 21:11.520
All silver coins, eh?

21:11.520 --> 21:13.160
Such ignorance.

21:13.160 --> 21:16.620
As expected of a backwater noble who 
won his title on the battlefield.

21:16.940 --> 21:19.950
This won't be enough to keep my mouth shut.

21:21.340 --> 21:24.260
No hard feelings, milord.

21:29.690 --> 21:31.500
<i>That refreshing tartness!</i>

21:31.500 --> 21:32.700
<i>It really is an apple!</i>

21:32.700 --> 21:34.310
<i>How many years has it been?!</i>

21:35.090 --> 21:36.040
Father?

21:37.080 --> 21:43.550
Let's not tell Mother or Sister 
that we ate the best ones.

21:45.450 --> 21:46.400
Good idea.

21:51.150 --> 21:53.390
<i>I'm gonna make an apple pie!</i>

21:53.390 --> 21:56.600
<i>And then tarts and candy apples...</i>

21:56.600 --> 21:58.290
<i>And then, one day...</i>

21:58.690 --> 22:00.640
<i>I'm going to make it!</i>

22:00.970 --> 22:04.270
<i>This world's very own land of sweets!</i>

23:37.160 --> 23:38.970
Next time on <i>Sweet Reincarnation</i>...

23:39.040 --> 23:45.000
<b>The Patissier and the Fief's Defense Line</b>

23:39.420 --> 23:41.550
"The Patissier and the Fief's Defense Line."

23:41.880 --> 23:43.210
Bon appétit!

23:45.000 --> 23:49.960
<b>Illustration:</b>

23:45.000 --> 23:49.960
<b>Yasuyuki Syuri</b>
